{"requirements":[{"id":"managed-service","requirement":"Run inventory-api on node1 as a managed service that serves requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"inventory-api was installed as an enabled systemd service, ran under a dedicated account, listened on port 8080, and returned HTTP 200 health responses. It remained enabled, active, and responsive after a node reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-84bc9a2bb00d4997","cmd-50e86f2507e34c32","cmd-2ce0d7bdf9da47dd","cmd-dfae33011bc44c24"]},{"id":"oom-survival","requirement":"Keep inventory-api serving when a memory-hungry process causes system-wide out-of-memory pressure, with the kernel stopping the memory hog rather than inventory-api.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before the test, inventory-api was healthy as PID 1657 with OOM adjustment -900. A bounded hog then consumed about 1.8 GiB and triggered a documented global OOM; the kernel killed hog PID 1729 with OOM adjustment 1000. Immediately afterward, inventory-api was still active with the unchanged PID 1657 and returned a healthy response.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e8fede217f5a4fee","cmd-8eeb3da8c4f44aea","cmd-5ec674cea5ce4b58"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account/directory creation, application and unit installation, and service enablement directly established the requested service (cmd-6c169cfbc95b41e5, cmd-84bc9a2bb00d4997, cmd-869e0d2581264da4). The transient memory hog was a bounded behavioral test (cmd-8eeb3da8c4f44aea), and its failed-state record and temporary script were removed afterward (cmd-2ce0d7bdf9da47dd). The reboot was required provider-wide evidence collection (cmd-8908b62693bc4d7b). Final lifecycle evidence shows no failed services, healthy package state, and no abandoned hog file; the added port 8080 listener and inventory-api private temporary directory are expected service state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6c169cfbc95b41e5","cmd-84bc9a2bb00d4997","cmd-869e0d2581264da4","cmd-8eeb3da8c4f44aea","cmd-2ce0d7bdf9da47dd","cmd-8908b62693bc4d7b","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. inventory-api is a functioning managed service, and a directly observed global OOM killed the designated memory hog while the API retained its PID and remained responsive. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and system, service, listener, health, and inventory state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["No HTTP request was captured at the exact instant the hog was still allocating memory because the hog was killed before the executor's planned during-pressure probe; continuity is instead demonstrated by the API's unchanged PID and successful responses immediately before and after the bounded global OOM event."]}
